## 3. Results

### 3.1 Smoke run (`data/smoke.json`)
2 cells, 2 Gy, default parameters, 240 min. Established the pipeline runs end-to-end. Default `k_on`/`k_clean` are too slow → only ~3% rejoining by 4 h. **Used to confirm code correctness, not to claim agreement with the paper.**

### 3.2 Tuned parameter sweep
| Run | Doses (Gy) | n_cells | t_end | Key params | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `tune1.json` | 2 | 5 | 24 h | `k_on=2`, `k_clean=0.4`, `D_t=1e-3`, `R_syn=50 nm` | "Diffusive" regime; mis-rejoin appears (24% of rejoins are mis); residual 57% at 24h (TOO HIGH vs literature 5%) |
| `tune2.json` | 2 | 5 | 24 h | `k_on=3`, `k_clean=0.5`, `D_t=1e-4`, `R_syn=50 nm` | "Tethered" regime; residual 2.6% at 24h (matches literature); no mis-rejoin (D too small) |
| `dose_response.json` | 0.5/1/2/5/10 | 8 | 24 h | tune2 params | Residual fraction at 24h: 0.8%/1.8%/2.6%/1.7%/2.0% (flat with dose) |
| `dose_response_misrejoin.json` | 0.5/1/2/5/10 | 8 | 24 h | tune1 params | Mis-rejoin fraction rises with dose: 1.6%/14%/25%/34%/47% |

