### 3.5 Figures
- `figures/fig1_rejoining_kinetics.png` — residual DSB fraction vs log time at 2 Gy for both scenarios, against a literature biexponential band (fast t½ 10–20 min, slow t½ 120–180 min, ~5% asymptote at 24 h; Rothkamm & Löbrich 2003; Karlsson & Stenerlöw 2004).
- `figures/fig2_residual_vs_dose.png` — residual DSB fraction at 24 h vs dose for both scenarios. Scenario B markedly overestimates residuals at low dose, matching the abstract's claim that "three of the model scenarios obviously overestimate residual DSBs after long-term repair after low-dose irradiation."
- `figures/fig3_misrejoin_vs_dose.png` — mis-rejoin fraction vs dose for both scenarios. Scenario B shows clear dose-dependence consistent with proximity-driven misrejoining; Scenario A is essentially zero (cognate ends always pair because diffusion is suppressed and `R_syn` is small).

